s</article-title><source>J. Mol. Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>328</volume><fpage>749</fpage><lpage>767</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12706730</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holm</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Sander</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mapping the protein universe</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1996</year><volume>273</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>603</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8662544</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>XQ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A space-efficient algorithm for local similarities</article-title><source>Comput. Appl. Biosci</source><year>1990</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>373</fpage><lpage>381</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2257499</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>John</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Human microRNA targets</article-title><source>PLoS Biol</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>e363</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15502875</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Domain assignment for protein structures using a consensus approach: characterization and analysis</article-title><source>Protein Sci</source><year>1998</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>233</fpage><lpage>242</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9521098</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koonin</surname><given-names>EV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Orthologs, paralogs, and evolutionary genomics</article-title><source>Annu. Rev. Genet</source><year>2005</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>309</fpage><lpage>338</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16285863</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krause</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Large scale hierarchical clustering of protein sequences</article-title><source>BMC Bioinformatics</source><year>2005</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>15</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15663796</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kriventseva</surname><given-names>EV</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Clustering and analysis of protein families</article-title><source>Curr. Opin. Struct. Biol</source><year>2001</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>334</fpage><lpage>339</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11406384</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kunin</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The properties of protein family space depend on experimental design</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2005</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>2618</fpage><lpage>2622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15769834</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B26"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lankester</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the use of the term homology in modern zoology</ar